			"id": 15,
			"title": "Recent error traces",
			"description": "Tempo traceql search for service.name=ktb with status=error, newest first. Tail sampling keeps ALL error traces, so this list is complete even though only ~15% of healthy traffic is stored. Click a trace to open it in Explore.",
			"datasource": {
				"type": "tempo",
				"uid": "tempo"
			},
			"gridPos": {
				"x": 0,
				"y": 41,
				"w": 24,
				"h": 10
			},
			"targets": [
				{
					"filters": [],
					"refId": "A",
					"queryType": "traceql",
					"query": "{ resource.service.name = \"ktb\" && status = error }",
					"tableType": "traces",
					"limit": 20
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "text",
			"transparent": false,
			"repeatDirection": "h",
			"options": {
				"mode": "markdown",
				"content": "Traces pass through a **tail_sampling** processor in the collector (`infra/lgtm/otelcol-config.yaml`):\n\n- **Keep** every trace containing an error span (`status_code = ERROR`)\n- **Keep** traces slower than **2s** end-to-end\n- **Sample** the remaining ~**15%** probabilistically\n\nMetrics are generated app-side (`effect/Metric` → OTLP metrics), **not** derived from traces — so sampling cannot skew the RED panels. For volume questions use metrics, not trace counts.\n\nSpan names include `app.run`, `app.runAs`, `queue.audio.transcribe`. Narrow searches with `{ span.http.route = \"...\" }`, `{ duration > 2s }` or `{ status = ok }`."
			},
			"id": 16,
			"title": "Tail sampling context",
			"description": "Why trace panels look sparse",
			"gridPos": {
				"x": 0,
				"y": 51,
				"w": 24,
				"h": 6
			}
		}
	]
